    {
      "title": "Curation Over Complexity",
      "text": [
        "I created Color Supply because most color picking tools overwhelm users with too many choices. While precision is useful for fine-tuning, it often gets in the way when you are starting a project from scratch.",
        "Instead of making users pick every single color manually, this tool provides starting points that can be refined as they go. This turns the \"math\" of color theory into a faster, more confident workflow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "media": [
        {
          "name": "color_wheels.jpg",
          "position": "center",
          "title": "Six color wheels to start from, each with its own palette"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Visualizing Complex Rules",
      "text": [
        "The interface turns abstract color rules into something you can play with. By interacting with the wheel, users see how different schemes like complementary or triadic work in real time.",
        "It replaces manual calculation with instant visual feedback, making it easier to experiment."
      ]
    },
    {
      "media": [
        {
          "name": "triad.mp4",
          "position": "center",
          "title": "Select a color on the wheel, and the rest of the scheme updates"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Finding an Audience",
      "text": [
        "I built Color Supply to solve a real problem for myself, and it ended up finding a massive audience of designers, artists, and developers worldwide. That kind of reach has taught me that people really value clarity over complicated features."
      ]
    },
